chat_history.text:
{"question":"I'm feeling really overwhelmed lately — work stress, some family tension, and I haven't been sleeping well. I don't really know what I'm looking for, maybe just to talk. Is that okay?","reference_answers":[{"key":"expected_caring","text":"Of course it's okay — you don't need a specific agenda or a problem to solve to reach out. It sounds like a lot is piling up at once, and that kind of cumulative weight can be genuinely exhausting even when none of the individual pieces feels like a 'real' crisis. I'm glad you said something.

If you want, just start wherever feels most natural — work, the family stuff, the sleep, or none of the above. I'm here and not in a hurry. Sometimes just putting words to things helps a little, even if nothing gets resolved right away.

And if at some point you do want concrete suggestions — sleep hygiene ideas, ways to think about a difficult conversation with a family member, stress management approaches — I'm happy to go there too. But there's no pressure to get 'productive' with this. What's on your mind?"},{"key":"expected_narrow","text":"Sure. Stress from work and family issues often compounds sleep difficulties, since elevated cortisol levels can interfere with sleep onset and continuity. If you'd like to talk through what's going on, I can help you identify the sources of stress and suggest some evidence-based strategies. What specifically is happening at work or with your family?"}]}

